			"notes": {
				"rationale": "＋ (U+FF0B) is a code point of its own, not a spelling of +: a Variant is a spelling that a standard accepts or once accepted, a dialect uses, or that stretches letters for effect, and a fullwidth form is none of these (de/variant-and-historical-status). It is a SYM Lemma of its own, Canonical, as the minus sign − (U+2212) is apart from the hyphen-minus. ＋ is the fullwidth plus sign and means what + means, so it copies the description of +. Segment fix decided by an agent under the user's delegation (2026-10-02, #853): the + the sentence names last was a Punctuation Segment and is now ResolvableText (de/sign-for-a-word). No target changed."
